@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# Pod 4 handoff
+
+Awaiting the final independent source review. Do not launch until the owner says “Pod 4 ready”.
+
+## Launch artifact
+
+- Pushed runtime source pin: `3b4b308f0a766a59775950331ae9cd30b848d47d`.
+- Source URL: https://github.com/oborchers/Fast_Sentence_Embeddings/commit/3b4b308f0a766a59775950331ae9cd30b848d47d
+- Script: `benchmarks/baseline/dr151_pod4_20261101.sh`.
+- Absolute script path: `/Users/oliverborchers/.herdr/worktrees/Fast_Sentence_Embeddings/dr151-compare/benchmarks/baseline/dr151_pod4_20261101.sh`.
+- SHA256: `cf5ff8d1952ce6995978dbdd7ac5f153efb7821b103693a5a5bebaccbada652b`.
+- Image and CPU: `python:3.13`, RunPod `cpu3c`, Linux x86_64, 32 assigned vCPUs. The actual CPU model is recorded on the pod, not assumed.
+- RAM: 64 GB. Container disk: 100 GB, with a capacity/free-space preflight.
+- Whole-script hard limit: 8,400 seconds (140 minutes), including setup and export. No benchmark starts locally.
+- Maximum planning cost: USD 2.55 at compute no greater than USD 1/hour, allowing 10 additional minutes for startup and result collection and prorated 100 GB storage at USD 0.10/GB/month. Actual console rate must satisfy this condition. Idle sleep after ALL_DONE continues billing.
+
+## Frozen stage list
+
+1. SSH setup, pinned Python environment and Rust worker build with explicit parallelism.
+2. Bounded long-call A/A host probe. Calibration plus probe has a 15-minute limit; the measured probe has a further three-minute limit. Require its explicit passing receipt before later work.
+3. README panels: all 21 encoding series. POTION-8M float32/float16/int8 table at 1/16/32; Model2Vec, model2vec-rs and FastEmbed paired with POTION-8M float32 at 1/16/32; native sentence-transformers StaticEmbedding paired with static-retrieval-mrl-en-v1 float32 at 1/16/32.
+4. Corrected folded classification: all 15 SetFit datasets plus FineWeb, workers 1/32. Same-head comparison of folded fse, explicit fse encode-plus-head and Model2Vec plus the same frozen head. Separately, the fine-tuned Model2Vec MLP exported to NumPy. Accuracy is measured on the original complete held-out splits.
+5. Final artifact export, independent receipt validation, then ALL_DONE and sleep.
+
+Table/selection inputs are shared per model. Each library bar uses its own calibrated paired workload, identical within the pair, with its count and digest retained. Inputs are labelled sampled and shuffled WikiText-103 passages, seed 0. Every actual published fse call must last at least two seconds. Require three accepted rotating rounds, own backend identity and A/A upper bound at most 1.10. All original raw observations remain available.
+
+No worker curve points 2/4/8, 10M write stage, 100M repeat, MIND or quality batch is included. The hard limit can leave partial classification coverage. Failed, missing, short or noisy cells cannot produce a successful final manifest. A failed quiet probe stops later spending.
+
+## Results and lifecycle ownership
+
+fse-main publishes the script, launches, monitors over SSH at least every 30 minutes, copies results after ALL_DONE, verifies transfer SHA256, then asks the owner before deletion. dr151-compare never launches, stops or deletes pods.
+
+Copy all text/JSON/log files under `/dr151-results`, preserving relative paths, including:
+
+- `/dr151-results/bootstrap.log` and `bootstrap-invocation.json`.
+- `/dr151-results/pod4-plan.json`, `disk-preflight.json`, `cache-ownership.json`, and stage-completion receipts.
+- `/dr151-results/readme-panels/probe.json` and `probe/speed-results.jsonl`.
+- `/dr151-results/readme-panels/plan.json`, `summary.json`, `calibration.jsonl`, `output-checks.jsonl`, `invocations.jsonl`, `speed-results.jsonl` and any other text receipts present.
+- `/dr151-results/folded-classification/classification-plan.json`, `classification-summary.json`, `classification-quality.jsonl`, `calibration.jsonl`, `invocations.jsonl`, `speed-results.jsonl`, and each dataset's `manifest.json` and other text receipts.
+
+Exclude model weights, caches, `.npy` vectors and every `pipeline-inputs` directory. These are regenerable. Actual input counts, digests and repetitions are embedded in operation records. DR190 artifact blocks in logs remain a fallback.
+
